    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d164">

                <pb facs="0218" n="200" sameAs="frus:frus1946v11/pg200"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">862.20235/2–846: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Argentina</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Cabot</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Buenos
                                Aires</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-02-08T11:00:00-03:00">February 8, 1946—11
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received February 8—9:30 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>415. ReEmbtel 403, February 6, 9
                        p.m.,<anchor n="43" xml:id="d164-f1"/> and Deptel 160, January 26, 2 p.m. I believe that Cooke is making real
                    effort to get as many Nazi agents as he can off on <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Highland Monarch</hi>. There appears good reason to suppose that Cooke is
                    genuinely concerned at what we may do and reveal, and that the principal
                    obstacles are anti-Perón courts dominated by conservatives which are looking
                    with decidedly jaundiced eye on war as well as other powers revolutionary
                    Government has sought to arrogate to itself.</p>
                <pb facs="0219" n="201" xml:id="pg201"/>
                <p>Under circumstances I doubt that drastic action or recriminations would be
                    justified on basis of failure to deliver agents under court order. Freude<anchor
                        n="44" xml:id="d164-f2"/> case is in somewhat different category despite
                    fact Court of Appeals has cleared way for securing Argentine citizenship.
                    Naturally if Government fails to deport any agents not under court order my
                    recommendation does not apply.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Cabot</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d164-f1" n="43" xml:id="d164-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d164-f2" n="44" xml:id="d164-f2-content">
                <p>Ludwig Freude, German-born head of Cía General de Construcciones, accused of
                    espionage in behalf of the Axis.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
